# Nightly database backup for visio.samourai.app — scripts/backup.sh.
#
# Install: replace <user> with the deploy user (must be in the docker group)
# and the two absolute paths, then:
#   sudo cp deploy/host/visio-backup.cron /etc/cron.d/visio-backup
#
# stdout goes to journald via logger; failures also leave a stale
# ~/backups/LAST_OK, which `preflight.sh stack` turns red within a day — the
# cron itself never fails silently.
#
# preflight.sh `config` asserts this file is installed and carries both
# lines: the dump, and the prune.
#
# Two processes, on purpose. The dump runs with the write key, which cannot
# delete; the prune runs with the delete key, in a process that never sees
# the dump. Same night, after the dump has landed and been verified, so the
# published 30-day retention holds to the day — a weekly prune would let a
# dump live up to 37 days against the number the privacy page publishes
# (and would need the +2 slack in backup.sh raised to cover the gap).
17 3 * * * <user> VISIO_DIR=<absolute path to ~/visio> <absolute path to the repo clone>/scripts/backup.sh 2>&1 | logger -t visio-backup
45 3 * * * <user> VISIO_DIR=<absolute path to ~/visio> <absolute path to the repo clone>/scripts/backup.sh prune 2>&1 | logger -t visio-backup
